   2932  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2933  f97a							; E4 moth exit tramp ($FC49-$FC4E) — bank2 executes `sta $1FF4` at $FC49
   2934  f97a							; (byte-identical slice, guard: verify_build), then the fetch at $FC4C comes
   2935  f97a							; from bank0 = `jmp UE_Next` (real label here — no cross-bank address sync).
   2936  f97a							; bank0's `sta $1FF4` copy never runs; bank2's bytes from $FC4C never run.
   2937  f97a							;
   2938  f97a							; MUST stay off $FFF6-$FFF9: those are the ONLY addresses in code space where
   2939  f97a							; (addr & $1FFF) lands in $1FF4-$1FF7 = F6 hotspot mirrors. Stella's
   2940  f97a							; CartridgeEnhanced::peek (CartEnh.cxx:157, ADDR_MASK=$1FFF) calls
   2941  f97a							; checkSwitchBank on READS — the old $FFF2 placement fetched the `jmp`
   2942  f97a							; operands at $FFF6/$FFF7 and flipped banks mid-instruction (operand hi from
   2943  f97a							; bank1 = $00 -> jmp $007D -> HUD runaway, 359/360-line frames, 5-byte stack
   2944  f97a							; leak per rogue Overscan entry -> SP decayed to $E1 -> frame-3 crash where
   2945  f97a							; jsr RefreshEnemyY's return landed on FetchPtr). Real F6 is write-only, but
   2946  f97a							; no fetched byte may ever sit in the mirror zone.
   2947  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2948  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2949  f97a							; Cross-bank call pads (docs/leaf_move_plan.md) — byte-identical copies live in
   2950  f97a							; bank1 at the SAME addresses. F6 hotspots switch on ANY write — the written
   2951  f97a							; value is ignored (proven by FoldIndirect's `sta $1FF4` carrying data bytes) —
   2952  f97a							; so the pads `sta $1FF5`/`sta $1FF4` with A AS-IS: A/X/Y/flags pass through
   2953  f97a							; unchanged, making the pad equivalent to the original inlined `jsr`.
   2954  f97a							; (2026-09-30 bug: `lda #1` before `sta $1FF5` clobbered A — ClearPFColumn
   2955  f97a							; punched col 1 instead of the bomb's col, AddScore added +1 instead of
   2956  f97a							; +50/+75. Hole appeared at screen col 1 + mirror col 18 = "second tile from
   2957  f97a							; each edge"; collision stayed correct because WallMask is separate.)
   2958  f97a							; `sta` does not touch flags — IsRoomDark's `beq` contract survives the
   2959  f97a							; return. Carry survives. No stack use.
   2960  f97a							; ==============================================================================
